NOTICE
======

No third-party source file is copied into this benchmark. Every
implementation it measures is fetched at run time from the repository and
commit recorded in pins.json.

Two files here are not merely callers of fetched code. arms/sglang_v1.py and
arms/sglang_v2.py transcribe the block-configuration selector logic of
sglang-jax (Apache-2.0) so that each SGLang arm runs at the configuration its
owner's own selector would return, and each transcription cites the file and
function it mirrors in the docstring beside it. The kit verifies those
mirrors against the pinned source at run time (the selector-mirror gate) and
refuses the run when a mirror and its source disagree. arms/_sglang.py is the
frame those two arms share and carries the same attribution.

arms/_sources.py performs the fetch. For each pins.json entry it initializes
a repository under arms/_sources/<entry name>, fetches the entry's ref from
the entry's repo, checks out the entry's commit, and hashes every file the
entry names. A file whose sha256 does not match the pinned value refuses the
run and prints the repository, the commit, the pinned hash and the file. An
arm therefore executes the pinned source or it executes nothing.

arms/_sources/ is not committed. The pins are the record, not the checkouts.

Where each fetched checkout lands, and whose license governs it. Every pin
below is fetched on any clone; the last three are fetched only when this
checkout cannot serve the arm itself, which is described under each.

